From: gdterm
Subject: [PATCH] nego: don't downgrade to legacy RDP security on LB/redirect when NLA is requested

When connecting through a Citrix NetScaler-style load balancer, the
backend server answers the security-layer negotiation with `li == 6`
("no rdpNegData") and a routing token in the Connection Confirm PDU.

The token-based redirection path (LB_LOAD_BALANCE_INFO) causes FreeRDP
to reconnect with the routing token, but on that reconnect the server
still replies with `li == 6`.  The existing code unconditionally falls
through to legacy RDP security:

    else if (li == 6)
    {
        WLog_DBG(TAG, "no rdpNegData");
        if (!nego->EnabledProtocols[PROTOCOL_RDP])
            nego->state = NEGO_STATE_FAIL;
        else
            nego->state = NEGO_STATE_FINAL;
    }

Because `nego_enable_nla()` only enables PROTOCOL_HYBRID and leaves
PROTOCOL_RDP enabled, a `/sec:nla` client ends up "negotiating" plain
RDP security.  NetScaler rejects the resulting legacy-RDP connection and
the server logs the user off (ERRINFO_LOGOFF_BY_USER / 0x0001000C).

This matches FreeRDP issue #1841 ("Token based redirection fails ...").

Fix: when a routing token is present (i.e. we are in the load-balancing /
redirection path) and NLA is one of the requested protocols, refuse the
downgrade instead of silently switching to legacy RDP security.  This has
no effect on genuine legacy RDP servers (which never carry a routing
token), so the old behaviour is fully preserved for them.

diff --git a/libfreerdp/core/nego.c b/libfreerdp/core/nego.c
index 5c3c54a..1f42b94 100644
--- a/libfreerdp/core/nego.c
+++ b/libfreerdp/core/nego.c
@@ -661,6 +661,9 @@ int nego_recv(rdpTransport* transport, wStream* s, void* extra)
 
 		if (!nego->EnabledProtocols[PROTOCOL_RDP])
 			nego->state = NEGO_STATE_FAIL;
+		else if ((nego->RoutingTokenLength > 0) &&
+		         nego->EnabledProtocols[PROTOCOL_HYBRID])
+			nego->state = NEGO_STATE_FAIL;
 		else
 			nego->state = NEGO_STATE_FINAL;
 	}
